after), but the set of contacted partners is virtually identical on both sides of the candidate change point (same ~30-node core; Jaccard \u2248 1.0). Partner-side activity is also flat across all sub-windows. Hence there is no old-contacts-to-new-contacts replacement: no regime switch of interaction partners, only member rotation onto a stationary neighbourhood."}, "raw_final_response": "**Analysis**\n\n- The group is highly active (~1100 events in the window, step_02/step_20) and its members appear among the top-active nodes (step_23) \u2014 a volume/popularity confounder, not evidence of a switch.\n- Group members activate in *disjoint* time blocks: 114 fires only in [45074,50074] (90 events, step_14), 356 in [50074,60074] (step_16), 1107 in [65074,70074] (step_15), 1268/1311 in [70074,75074] (step_19). So the *membership* rotates over time (step_03 vs step_04), which superficially looks like a change point around t\u224860000 (activity dip, step_05/step_07).\n- But the **partner sets are the same on both sides**. 114 @[45074,50074] \u2192 {40,61,63,80,116,184,239,250,327,338,349,493,515,749,785,897,912,918,924,926,1110,1348,1355,1505,1526,1593,1750,1760,1792,1922} (step_17); 654 @[45074,60074] and 140 @[45074,60074] essentially the same list (step_22, step_25); 356 @[55000,60000] the same (step_10); and after the candidate change point 731 (step_09), 959 (step_11), 1107 (step_18), 1268 (step_24), 1311 (step_21) contact that *identical* 30-node core. Jaccard(before, after) \u2248 1.0 (step_28).\n- The core partners' own activity is flat across all six sub-windows (211/240/157/164/213/211, step_20) \u2014 no partner-side turnover either.\n\nSo there is no old-set \u2192 new-set replacement; the group's neighbourhood is stationary. The apparent discontinuity is member rotation onto a fixed contact core, not a regime switch of interaction partners.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8155967f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"en